Rebased to latest the old hunks were dead, as you say. The guard is now applied once in l2_transfer.py:123-127:
  
  for indices in (transfer.host_indices, transfer.device_indices):
       if indices.device.type != "cpu":
           indices.record_stream(stream)
  
Both directions covered via the callers at :71 and :112; the cache_controller.py hunks are dropped. pool_host/common.py is rebased onto the new allocator / registration_granularity_bytes signature.
  
Covered by test/registered/unit/mem_cache/test_l2_transfer_record_stream.py (base-a-test-cpu, 2 cases) — reverting to is_cuda turn

Fixed. The rebase moved this into L2TransferEngine._record_stream (l2_transfer.py:122-127), and the added
  comment is dropped — the method is now just:
  
   @staticmethod
   def _record_stream(transfers: list[L2Transfer], stream) -> None:
       for transfer in transfers:
           for indices in (transfer.host_indices, transfer.device_indices):
               if indices.device.type != "cpu":
                   indices.record_stream(stream)
  
 The method name and the pre-existing rationale carry it; nothing in the diff needed narrating. The cache_controller.py hunk this comment was attached to no longer exists.

